More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (911–920)
911. Improper Validation of API Authentication Headers
Authentication Header Manipulation
Applications incorrectly trust authentication headers, allowing attackers to impersonate users.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
912. Insecure Handling of Session Tokens in URLs
Session Token Exposure
Session tokens appear in URLs and can be captured through logs or referrer headers.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
913. Improper Validation of Organization Membership APIs
Organization Membership Bypass
Attackers add themselves to organizations or teams without proper permission.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
914. Insecure Handling of Data Backup Endpoints
Backup Endpoint Exposure
Backup endpoints expose sensitive user data or system configurations.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
915. Improper Validation of File Deletion APIs
File Deletion Authorization Bypass
Attackers delete files belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
916. Insecure Handling of Application Debug Interfaces
Debug Interface Exposure
Debug interfaces expose internal system details or allow command execution.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
917. Improper Validation of Social Login APIs
Social Login Authentication Bypass
Attackers manipulate OAuth responses to access other accounts.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
918. Insecure Handling of API File Upload Logs
Upload Log Data Exposure
File upload logs expose file paths or sensitive metadata.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $5,000
919. Improper Validation of Messaging APIs
Messaging API Authorization Bypass
Attackers read or send messages belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
920. Insecure Handling of API Error Messages
Verbose Error Message Exposure
Detailed error messages reveal sensitive information about backend systems.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
✅ Most profitable vulnerabilities on platforms like HackerOne and Bugcrowd still include:
Remote Code Execution
SQL Injection
Server-Side Request Forgery
Broken Access Control
Cross-Site Scripting
Tools often used to discover them include Burp Suite, OWASP ZAP, Nmap, and FFUF.
